  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday) \nIssued at 1028 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThe FA will remain under the influence of the upper level ridge \nthrough the first half of the extended period, with the ridge axis \nshifting back westward and becoming more amplified Wednesday. This \nblocking pattern will be supported by a closed low developing near \nthe Carolina coastline, while a secondary closed low over the PacNW \ndigs southward toward Baja California. Increasing geopotential \nheights and thickness values, along with continued WAA from \nsouthwesterly flow aloft and lee surface troughing, will continue \nto support the gradual warming trend through the week. Temperatures \nwill climb above seasonal normals by Wednesday, with highs in the \nupper 70s to mid 80s. Along with the warming afternoon temperatures, \nwe can also expect the drier trend to continue as well through much \nof the work week. \n\nHeading into the weekend, guidance continues to hint at a potential \nreturn of precipitation as the upper level pattern begins to evolve. \nHowever, considerable differences remain among deterministic \nguidance regarding the timing and progression of the broader trough, \nwith the ECMWF favoring a more progressive solution while the GFS \ndevelops a closed low near the base of the trough. Despite these \ndifferences, ensemble guidance continues to suggest some potential \nfor precipitation across much of the region. Given the vast amount \nof uncertainty surrounding the evolution of the system with it being \nseveral days out, will continue to monitor trends as new guidance \nbecomes available and in better agreement. For now, will maintain",
